{
  "ideas": [
    {
      "id": 8,
      "name": "Climb",
      "approach": "handmade",
      "approachWhy": "Every climb must be tuned against the real climb speed and the drip beat, and the good shapes (stacked ladders, hanging ladders, chimneys, a tower spiral) are few and distinct. A generator would mostly reshuffle heights and make drip timing unfair, so each variant is hand-made.",
      "engine": {
        "have": [
          "Climbable ladders: shape \"truss\" (StickyLadder already does ladder, ledge, jump, ladder)",
          "Ledge and pillar slabs, and a section that ends higher than it starts (rise)",
          "Course tests that skip the jump-rise check for ladder steps (special = \"climb\")",
          "slide motion (for a ladder that moves sideways) with phase offsets",
          "Fall back to the start pad when you drop under the lowest platform"
        ],
        "new": [
          {
            "what": "Hazard touch = back to the start pad (the shared item from idea 1 Crusher Alley; build once for all hazard ideas)",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "drip motion kind: a red see-through drop swells at a dark nozzle for about 1 s with a gurgle, falls straight down the climb, splats, repeats on period and phase at server time (idea 22's 'Goo Drip' slides down a wall on slide motion instead; same drop look, so make one drop prop for both)",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Ladder look: an open lattice of lime jelly rungs you can see through (a real ladder shape), a squelch-pop per rung while you climb. Must NOT be the flat dripping goo sheet with handprints, because idea 22 Sticky Walls owns that look and its walls slide you down",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Test step kind \"grab\": jump from a ledge into a ladder hanging over the void (reach check to the ladder face, not to a floor)",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Moving ladder: reuse idea 3's 'ride' motion (move between stops, wait at each) so the ladder sits still while lined up. Slide motion already carries a standing player; check in Studio whether a climbing one is carried too, and if not the client carries them",
            "size": "M"
          },
          {
            "what": "Crumbling ladder piece: idea 2's melt trigger and 'melt warning look' (cracks, darkening, speeding crack sound) on a truss piece, starting when you grab it; comes back after a few seconds",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Landing tell for drips that hit pillar tops: reuse idea 1's growing floor shadow",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Section length cap raised from 36 to about 100 studs in the tests (shared with the other long ideas)",
            "size": "S"
          }
        ]
      },
      "readability": "You can climb only the open lattice ladders with lime jelly rungs; plain grey walls and pillars are not climbable, and flat dripping goo sheets are idea 22's sticky walls, not ladders. Red see-through drops swell at a dark nozzle with a gurgle for about a second before they fall, so you see and hear the beat before you commit; a crumbling ladder cracks and darkens from the moment you grab it.",
      "generator": null,
